# Configuration, as of 19 Oct 2026, lives on the secret server, not here.
#
# appsettings.Dev.json carries Oracle:DefaultPasswordBase64, which is a live
# credential for all seven instances. The others carry connection strings and
# host names. None of it belongs in the repo.
#
# Keep your local copies in EWT.Api/ where they have always been: the build reads
# them from there and a publish copies the one for the target environment into the
# dist as appsettings.json. They are simply no longer tracked.
#
# A fresh clone has none of them and will not publish until you fetch them from the
# secret server. appsettings.example.json is tracked and shows the shape.
appsettings.json
appsettings.Dev.json
appsettings.Test.json
appsettings.Prod.json
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.local.json
*.secrets.json
!appsettings.example.json

# Role-mining output contains staff email addresses (identity join key).
# Decide deliberately before committing personal data.
analysis/

# Timestamped copies the API keeps when a package fragment is edited at runtime.
OurPackages/**/*.bak
